<h1 class="page-title">Natural or Built</h1>
<p class="page-intro">
  The same landscape can be three different things. Some of these photographs
  were made in country that was left to itself, some in the built world, and
  some — the ones that interest me most — in the ground between, where a
  reservoir stands in for a lake and a line of groynes has been driven into a
  beach.
</p>
<p class="page-intro">
  This describes the <em>environment</em>, never the subject standing in it. A
  balloon over the Mara and a Mustang over Bray are both filed as Natural,
  because the savannah and the sky are, whatever is crossing them.
</p>
